{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol | sed -n '55,145p'; nl -ba packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol | sed -n '205,240p'; nl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/Clones.sol | sed -n '25,95p'; nl -ba packages/contracts/hardhat.config.ts | sed -n '1,150p'\"","aggregated_output":"    55\t\n    56\t    // Constructor\n    57\t\n    58\t    /// @notice Deploys the ownerless factory and its locked raffle implementation with one immutable configuration.\n    59\t    /// @dev The quote token must report exactly six decimals; the wrapper and quote token must contain deployed code.\n    60\t    ///      Deployment tooling must supply and verify the target chain's official USDC address because the constructor\n    61\t    ///      cannot prove token identity from metadata.\n    62\t    /// @param quoteToken_ Target chain's official six-decimal USDC contract trusted by every raffle.\n    63\t    /// @param vrfWrapper_ Official Chainlink VRF v2.5 native direct-funding wrapper for the target chain.\n    64\t    /// @param protocolTreasury_ Immutable protocol-fee recipient used by every raffle.\n    65\t    constructor(address quoteToken_, address vrfWrapper_, address protocolTreasury_) {\n    66\t        _requireContract(quoteToken_);\n    67\t        _requireContract(vrfWrapper_);\n    68\t        if (protocolTreasury_ == address(0)) revert ZeroAddress();\n    69\t\n    70\t        uint8 quoteDecimals = 0;\n    71\t        try IERC20Metadata(quoteToken_).decimals() returns (uint8 decimals_) {\n    72\t            quoteDecimals = decimals_;\n    73\t        } catch {\n    74\t            revert UnsupportedQuoteToken(quoteToken_);\n    75\t        }\n    76\t        if (quoteDecimals != RaffleConstants.QUOTE_TOKEN_DECIMALS) {\n    77\t            revert InvalidQuoteTokenDecimals(quoteDecimals, RaffleConstants.QUOTE_TOKEN_DECIMALS);\n    78\t        }\n    79\t\n    80\t        if (protocolTreasury_ == address(this) || protocolTreasury_ == quoteToken_ || protocolTreasury_ == vrfWrapper_)\n    81\t        {\n    82\t            revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(protocolTreasury_);\n    83\t        }\n    84\t\n    85\t        quoteToken = quoteToken_;\n    86\t        vrfWrapper = vrfWrapper_;\n    87\t        protocolTreasury = protocolTreasury_;\n    88\t\n    89\t        address implementation = address(new Raffle(quoteToken_, vrfWrapper_));\n    90\t        if (protocolTreasury_ == implementation) revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(protocolTreasury_);\n    91\t        raffleImplementation = implementation;\n    92\t    }\n    93\t\n    94\t    // External state-changing functions\n    95\t\n    96\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffleFactory\n    97\t    function createRaffle(CreateRaffleParams calldata params) external override nonReentrant returns (address raffle) {\n    98\t        _validateCreateParams(params);\n    99\t        uint256 currentTime = block.timestamp;\n   100\t        if (params.endTime <= currentTime) revert InvalidEndTime(currentTime, params.endTime);\n   101\t        uint256 saleDuration = uint256(params.endTime) - currentTime;\n   102\t        if (saleDuration > RaffleConstants.MAX_SALE_DURATION) {\n   103\t            revert SaleDurationTooLong(saleDuration, RaffleConstants.MAX_SALE_DURATION);\n   104\t        }\n   105\t        uint256 raffleId = ++raffleCount;\n   106\t        raffle = Clones.clone(raffleImplementation);\n   107\t        // The fresh fixed-target clone can initialize only once; this function is nonReentrant and atomic.\n   108\t        // slither-disable-next-line reentrancy-no-eth\n   109\t        IRaffle(raffle)\n   110\t            .initialize(\n   111\t                IRaffle.RaffleInitParams({\n   112\t                sponsor: msg.sender,\n   113\t                sponsorRecipient: params.sponsorRecipient,\n   114\t                protocolTreasury: protocolTreasury,\n   115\t                prizeToken: params.prizeToken,\n   116\t                prizeTokenId: params.prizeTokenId,\n   117\t                raffleId: raffleId,\n   118\t                reserveEntries: params.reserveEntries,\n   119\t                endTime: params.endTime\n   120\t            })\n   121\t            );\n   122\t\n   123\t        raffleById[raffleId] = raffle;\n   124\t        idByRaffle[raffle] = raffleId;\n   125\t        isRaffle[raffle] = true;\n   126\t\n   127\t        IERC721 prize = IERC721(params.prizeToken);\n   128\t        prize.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, raffle, params.prizeTokenId);\n   129\t        if (prize.ownerOf(params.prizeTokenId) != raffle) {\n   130\t            revert PrizeEscrowVerificationFailed(raffle, params.prizeToken, params.prizeTokenId);\n   131\t        }\n   132\t        if (IRaffle(raffle).status() != IRaffle.Status.Active) {\n   133\t            revert PrizeEscrowVerificationFailed(raffle, params.prizeToken, params.prizeTokenId);\n   134\t        }\n   135\t\n   136\t        emit RaffleCreated(\n   137\t            raffleId,\n   138\t            raffle,\n   139\t            msg.sender,\n   140\t            params.sponsorRecipient,\n   141\t            params.prizeToken,\n   142\t            params.prizeTokenId,\n   143\t            quoteToken,\n   144\t            protocolTreasury,\n   145\t            params.reserveEntries,\n    25\t     *\n    26\t     * This function uses the create opcode, which should never revert.\n    27\t     *\n    28\t     * WARNING: This function does not check if `implementation` has code. A clone that points to an address\n    29\t     * without code cannot be initialized. Initialization calls may appear to be successful when, in reality, they\n    30\t     * have no effect and leave the clone uninitialized, allowing a third party to initialize it later.\n    31\t     */\n    32\t    function clone(address implementation) internal returns (address instance) {\n    33\t        return clone(implementation, 0);\n    34\t    }\n    35\t\n    36\t    /**\n    37\t     * @dev Same as {xref-Clones-clone-address-}[clone], but with a `value` parameter to send native currency\n    38\t     * to the new contract.\n    39\t     *\n    40\t     * WARNING: This function does not check if `implementation` has code. A clone that points to an address\n    41\t     * without code cannot be initialized. Initialization calls may appear to be successful when, in reality, they\n    42\t     * have no effect and leave the clone uninitialized, allowing a third party to initialize it later.\n    43\t     *\n    44\t     * NOTE: Using a non-zero value at creation will require the contract using this function (e.g. a factory)\n    45\t     * to always have enough balance for new deployments. Consider exposing this function under a payable method.\n    46\t     */\n    47\t    function clone(address implementation, uint256 value) internal returns (address instance) {\n    48\t        if (address(this).balance < value) {\n    49\t            revert Errors.InsufficientBalance(address(this).balance, value);\n    50\t        }\n    51\t        assembly (\"memory-safe\") {\n    52\t            // Cleans the upper 96 bits of the `implementation` word, then packs the first 3 bytes\n    53\t            // of the `implementation` address with the bytecode before the address.\n    54\t            mstore(0x00, or(shr(232, shl(96, implementation)), 0x3d602d80600a3d3981f3363d3d373d3d3d363d73000000))\n    55\t            // Packs the remaining 17 bytes of `implementation` with the bytecode after the address.\n    56\t            mstore(0x20, or(shl(120, implementation), 0x5af43d82803e903d91602b57fd5bf3))\n    57\t            instance := create(value, 0x09, 0x37)\n    58\t        }\n    59\t        if (instance == address(0)) {\n    60\t            revert Errors.FailedDeployment();\n    61\t        }\n    62\t    }\n    63\t\n    64\t    /**\n    65\t     * @dev Deploys and returns the address of a clone that mimics the behavior of `implementation`.\n    66\t     *\n    67\t     * This function uses the create2 opcode and a `salt` to deterministically deploy\n    68\t     * the clone. Using the same `implementation` and `salt` multiple times will revert, since\n    69\t     * the clones cannot be deployed twice at the same address.\n    70\t     *\n    71\t     * WARNING: This function does not check if `implementation` has code. A clone that points to an address\n    72\t     * without code cannot be initialized. Initialization calls may appear to be successful when, in reality, they\n    73\t     * have no effect and leave the clone uninitialized, allowing a third party to initialize it later.\n    74\t     */\n    75\t    function cloneDeterministic(address implementation, bytes32 salt) internal returns (address instance) {\n    76\t        return cloneDeterministic(implementation, salt, 0);\n    77\t    }\n    78\t\n    79\t    /**\n    80\t     * @dev Same as {xref-Clones-cloneDeterministic-address-bytes32-}[cloneDeterministic], but with\n    81\t     * a `value` parameter to send native currency to the new contract.\n    82\t     *\n    83\t     * WARNING: This function does not check if `implementation` has code. A clone that points to an address\n    84\t     * without code cannot be initialized. Initialization calls may appear to be successful when, in reality, they\n    85\t     * have no effect and leave the clone uninitialized, allowing a third party to initialize it later.\n    86\t     *\n    87\t     * NOTE: Using a non-zero value at creation will require the contract using this function (e.g. a factory)\n    88\t     * to always have enough balance for new deployments. Consider exposing this function under a payable method.\n    89\t     */\n    90\t    function cloneDeterministic(\n    91\t        address implementation,\n    92\t        bytes32 salt,\n    93\t        uint256 value\n    94\t    ) internal returns (address instance) {\n    95\t        if (address(this).balance < value) {\n     1\timport hardhatToolboxViemPlugin from \"@nomicfoundation/hardhat-toolbox-viem\";\n     2\timport { configVariable, defineConfig } from \"hardhat/config\";\n     3\t\n     4\texport default defineConfig({\n     5\t  plugins: [hardhatToolboxViemPlugin],\n     6\t  paths: {\n     7\t    sources: \"./src\",\n     8\t    tests: {\n     9\t      nodejs: \"./test/hardhat\",\n    10\t    },\n    11\t    cache: \"./cache/hardhat\",\n    12\t    artifacts: \"./artifacts\",\n    13\t  },\n    14\t  solidity: {\n    15\t    profiles: {\n    16\t      default: {\n    17\t        version: \"0.8.36\",\n    18\t        settings: {\n    19\t          optimizer: {\n    20\t            enabled: true,\n    21\t            runs: 200,\n    22\t          },\n    23\t          evmVersion: \"cancun\",\n    24\t        },\n    25\t      },\n    26\t      production: {\n    27\t        version: \"0.8.36\",\n    28\t        settings: {\n    29\t          optimizer: {\n    30\t            enabled: true,\n    31\t            runs: 200,\n    32\t          },\n    33\t          evmVersion: \"cancun\",\n    34\t        },\n    35\t      },\n    36\t    },\n    37\t  },\n    38\t  networks: {\n    39\t    hardhatEthereum: {\n    40\t      type: \"edr-simulated\",\n    41\t      chainType: \"l1\",\n    42\t      chainId: 31_337,\n    43\t    },\n    44\t    sepolia: {\n    45\t      type: \"http\",\n    46\t      chainType: \"l1\",\n    47\t      chainId: 11_155_111,\n    48\t      url: configVariable(\"SEPOLIA_RPC_URL\"),\n    49\t      accounts: [configVariable(\"DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY\")],\n    50\t    },\n    51\t    mainnet: {\n    52\t      type: \"http\",\n    53\t      chainType: \"l1\",\n    54\t      chainId: 1,\n    55\t      url: configVariable(\"ETHEREUM_RPC_URL\"),\n    56\t      accounts: [configVariable(\"DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY\")],\n    57\t    },\n    58\t  },\n    59\t});\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"_kritt_extractor_helper\": true,\n  \"stub\": false,\n  \"stub_explanation\": \"\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Returns the configured wrapper's native VRF price for 300,000 callback gas and one random word, using the call's gas-price context.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:436 Raffle.getVrfRequestPrice - Public view entrypoint accepts no ABI arguments and performs no authorization or lifecycle checks.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:437 Raffle.getVrfRequestPrice - Calls the deployment-fixed i_vrfV2PlusWrapper through STATICCALL with callbackGasLimit = 300_000 and numWords = 1; the gas-limit constant is defined in packages/contracts/src/libraries/RaffleConstants.sol:39.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/vrf/dev/interfaces/IVRFV2PlusWrapper.sol:33 IVRFV2PlusWrapper.calculateRequestPriceNative - External pricing boundary returns uint256; documentation at line 27 specifies transaction gas-price dependence. The wrapper implementation is absent from the supplied snapshot.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:437 Raffle.getVrfRequestPrice - Decodes the successful wrapper response into fee and returns it unchanged to the caller.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Return the ABI-encoded uint256 native-token fee without state mutation, payment, randomness request, or asynchronous continuation.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 437,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The caller supplies execution gas-price context, preserved through clone delegation and the wrapper STATICCALL. Wrapper calldata contains only fixed arguments (300_000, 1); the caller cannot select the wrapper address or pricing arguments through this entrypoint.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"This external-call boundary trusts the immutable wrapper's quote and returns it without adjustment. Review concerns are gas-price context and dependency pricing semantics; internal wrapper pricing branches cannot be established from the supplied interface.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"If the configured wrapper reverts during the price query, the getter propagates that failure and returns no quote.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:436 Raffle.getVrfRequestPrice - Any external caller reaches the getter without authorization or lifecycle checks.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:437 Raffle.getVrfRequestPrice - Issues the external view call to the immutable wrapper with fixed arguments (300_000, 1) and the execution gas-price context.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/vrf/dev/interfaces/IVRFV2PlusWrapper.sol:33 IVRFV2PlusWrapper.calculateRequestPriceNative - External dependency boundary; a reverting response follows the failure outcome. Specific wrapper rejection conditions are unavailable in this snapshot.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:437 Raffle.getVrfRequestPrice - The high-level call has no try/catch or fallback quote, so the wrapper revert propagates to the external caller.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert the getter call with the wrapper failure; no fee is returned and no state changes occur.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 437,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The caller-controlled gas-price context reaches the same fixed wrapper invocation. The supplied code does not establish which gas-price values or wrapper conditions cause rejection.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"Quote availability depends directly on the external wrapper because failures are uncaught. This identifies the failure-propagation boundary without assuming unsupported internal checks or a caller-triggerable vulnerability.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}}
